# --- Per-run working directories for the ChEBI identification method ----------
#
# The method is documented in CHEBI_IDENTIFICATION.md and its reusable parts live
# in structure_check/, cas_registry.py and chebi_terms/. Everything one run produces
# is either a regenerable network cache or data derived from a single input
# spreadsheet, so none of it belongs in history: a finished run is a few MB of TSV
# answering a question nobody will ask again in that exact form.
#
# One pattern, and a run directory has to be named to match it. That is not just
# tidiness: the ruff pre-commit hooks lint all of bcp/ with no file list, so a run
# directory outside this pattern puts its throwaway scripts into `ruff check bcp/`
# and blocks every commit until they are clean. Name it chebi_run_<something>
# rather than adding a second pattern here.
chebi_run_*/

# Bulk artifacts, in case a run directory is deliberately kept under another name.
#
# Written without the `**/` prefix that the deliverables below also omit: a pattern
# containing no slash already matches at any depth, so the two forms were one rule
# written two ways. `master.tsv` is generic enough to catch an unrelated file some
# day -- `git check-ignore -v <path>` says why a path is ignored and `git add -f`
# overrides it.
.cache_pubchem.json
.cache_chebi.json
master.tsv
chebi_submission*.sdf

# Deliverables: communication artifacts addressed to ChEBI, the Lattice DB and
# the experimental team, with a date on them. Not source.
verified_chebi.tsv
unverified_chebi.tsv
chebi_submissions.tsv
lab_followup.tsv
